?rva006C39F0@Rva006C39F0Owner@@QAE_NIIIPAX@Z	0x006C39F0	191	partial	Insert-length roles corrected from the retail disassembly and the sete removed. Three source corrections this pass, all read off 0x006C39F0. (1) THE INSERT LENGTH IS NOT WHAT THE BANK HAD. The bank passed altLen on the direct path and allocSize on the allocated path. The bytes say otherwise: arg1 is loaded once into edi at 0x6C3A13 and is still live for the chain compare at 0x6C3A30, and the direct-buffer branch at 0x6C3A46 reaches the shared insert at 0x6C3A70 WITHOUT reloading edi, so arg1 is the direct-path length; only the allocated path reloads edi at 0x6C3A6A with arg2, while arg3 (allocSize) sizes the run and both trailing length words. arg1 therefore doubles as hash key and direct-path length, which is why it must stay live in a callee-save across the walk. Writing insertLen = key on the direct path and insertLen = altLen on the allocated path puts arg1 in edi exactly as retail has it, and is what pulls the chain compare into cmp DWORD PTR [edx],edi against retail rather than the bank esi. (2) owned = run == 0 replaced by a literal owned = 0, which drops the push ebx / sete bl MSVC emitted for the comparison. STILL OPEN and unchanged in kind: the PROLOGUE REGISTER PLAN. Retail is push ecx / mov al,[ecx+0x680] / test al,al / push ebx / mov [esp+4],ecx / mov bl,1 / je -- ebx is the FIRST callee-save, allocated in the prologue for owned, and ebp/edi/esi are pushed later IN THE BODY (0x6C3A06, 0x6C3A12, 0x6C3A3B) as each first becomes live. This body hoists every callee-save into the prologue (push ebp / push edi / push esi) and only allocates ebx for owned in the body at 0x6C3A2E, so every frame slot from the this-spill down is displaced and the whole stream stays one push out of phase even though from 0x6C3A30 on it is instruction for instruction retail. The cause is that MSVC 7.1 constant-folds owned to a literal on both paths that reach the shared done label (the tracking-off path and the ke